{'question': {':question/id': '61bbcb11-a041-5904-99b3-0554eb9f6731', ':question/problem': 'Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z &=-1 \\\\ y-2z &=3 \\\\ -5x+15y-5z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.', ':question/worked-solution': 'The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 15 & -5 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 15 & -5 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$', ':question/difficulty': ':question.difficulty/hard', ':question/answer-fields': [{':answer-field/id': '80fa0bef-1fa1-5c62-b5c5-36338c1f7b14', ':answer-field/key': 'selection', ':answer-field/type': ':answer-field.type/radio', ':answer-field/choices': [{':answer/id': '6ecf9a8f-4294-509f-bb3e-62dd25427f48', ':answer/type': ':answer.type/math', ':answer/value': '\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}'}, {':answer/id': '6a4a2508-f628-5c49-b5f1-220d6f7f3d23', ':answer/type': ':answer.type/math', ':answer/value': '\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}'}, {':answer/id': 'b252776b-bd3f-5299-927e-59e10aababab', ':answer/type': ':answer.type/math', ':answer/value': '\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}'}, {':answer/id': 'cfb69dda-7dad-5dc7-84b6-5a2c0ca6d3c5', ':answer/type': ':answer.type/math', ':answer/value': '\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}'}, {':answer/id': '7365c2e6-94dc-5e2e-8239-67660d1775b8', ':answer/type': ':answer.type/math', ':answer/value': '\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}'}], ':answer-field/correct': [':answer/id', '6a4a2508-f628-5c49-b5f1-220d6f7f3d23']}]}, 'knowledge_point': {'id': 'b010a518-7aa3-5b53-9a6d-ef0779ff0dfa', 'db_id': 17592186096745, 'title': 'Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a Singular 3x3 System With Two Pivots'}, 'generation': {'generator_id': '2e9ff447-ce56-57e5-9148-e9e03cc0f3aa', 'version': 'two-pivot-affine-v2', 'source_question': '8e9b3735-f721-557c-bd19-98de1fb72ed8', 'source_db_id': 17592186642343, 'source_basis': 5370, 'dependencies': {'sympy': '1.14.0'}, 'mathematical_fingerprint': '83da8f7868d85c22d145b2ed595ae1f1e6b6ba450172903972b8d57efb634ee6', 'seed': 0, 'template': 'q-74625', 'profile': 'q-74625', 'replay': True, 'parameters': {'original_parameters': True}, 'math_format': 'course-academy-tex-v1'}}
